Submitted By:            MVDW-Java
Date:                    2026-11-15
Initial Package Version: 5.4.1
Upstream Status:         Fixed upstream in gawk-5.4-stable (commit bf85f8a31),
                         not yet in a release. See bug-gawk 2026-09 msg00086
                         and 2026-07 msg00027.
Origin:                  Upstream fix (reconstructed as the single-line removal
                         Arnold Robbins confirmed as the correct fix)
Description:             gawk 5.4.1 built without MPFR/GMP: an array element
                         that does not exist yet, once tested in a comparison
                         (if (a["x"] == "") ...), reads back as the string "0"
                         instead of "" when used in string context.
                         This corrupts GCC 16.2's option generation
                         (gcc/optc-gen.awk), producing options.cc with
                           #error 0W<optname> does not have a Var() flag
                         (75 occurrences) and failing the GCC build at
                         options.o.

diff -Naur gawk-5.4.1.orig/awk.h gawk-5.4.1/awk.h
--- gawk-5.4.1.orig/awk.h	2026-11-15 09:57:25.092000000 +0100
+++ gawk-5.4.1/awk.h	2026-11-15 09:57:25.128000000 +0100
@@ -2049,7 +2049,6 @@
 
 	if ((s->flags & STRCUR) != 0
 		&& (s->stfmt == STFMT_UNUSED || (s->stfmt == fmtidx
-						&& (s->flags & (CONVFMT_FMT|OFMT_FMT)) == fmtflag
 #ifdef HAVE_MPFR
 						&& s->strndmode == MPFR_round_mode
 #endif
